      "message": "I don\u0027t think we can skip checking this when reset the sampler state. I think we should check that in `reset` and either construct a new GrSamplerState (that shouldn\u0027t have anisotropic filtering) or do the copy assignment if it\u0027s not restricted.\n\nI also think that this old `clamp_filter` function is incorrectly implemented, since this restriction pertains to disabling mipmapping (and by extension anisotropic filtering). We used to have mipmapping part of the `Filter` enum, but now it\u0027s a separate mode.  That is what should be being reset as well if the type is restricted. That is trivial to fix with the change I suggested above.",
